{
  "name": "nav-det (app chrome: sidebar nav + topbar + user menu + command palette, operator + builder, builder-cluster gating asserted)",
  "stopOnError": false,
  "notes": [
    "Code-verified against components/app/{Sidebar,Topbar,UserMenu}.svelte + ui/command/{Command,CommandItem}.svelte + keyboard/globalShortcuts.ts.",
    "Builder cluster (nav-llm, nav-transcriptions, sidebar-builder-separator, sidebar-builder-cluster-label) renders only when uiMode === 'builder' (Sidebar.svelte {#if isBuilder}). In operator mode it is asserted ABSENT via waitGone.",
    "Command palette items carry interpolated ids `command-item-{action-id}` (CommandItem.svelte); the old exact `command-item` no longer exists, so a generic item is matched via testidPrefix.",
    "topbar-search click dispatches Cmd+K, which globalShortcuts.ts TOGGLES; a second click closes the palette.",
    "user-menu-about navigates to the About settings sub-page (UserMenu.goAbout -> navigateToSettings('about')); there is no About dialog, so the landing is asserted on about-section and there is nothing to close.",
    "topbar-agents-at-work renders only when running tasks > 0 (data-dependent) and topbar-sidebar-toggle only when sidebarState === 'drawer' (mobile viewport). Both are observed by screenshot only, never hard-asserted."
  ],
